  "tour": {
    "title": "John’s New Creation and Genesis Allusions",
    "intro": "This tour traces how John tells Jesus’ story as a Genesis-shaped new creation. You will hear the opening “in the beginning,” then follow John’s light, tabernacle, seven-day, eighth-day, garden, and Spirit imagery toward the Bible’s final picture of renewed creation.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "recordId": "bibleproject:podcast:why-are-there-4-gospels",
        "startSec": 1960,
        "endSec": 2100,
        "why": "Start with John’s unmistakable opening signal. The hosts call “In the beginning” “the beginning of the new creation story” and say John wants readers to have “Genesis uploaded,” then connect John 1:3 with Genesis 1 and Proverbs 8.",
        "episodeTitle": "Why Are There Four Accounts of the Gospel?",
        "sourceId": "bibleproject",
        "source": "BibleProject",
        "audioUrl": "https://afp-597195-injected.calisto.simplecastaudio.com/695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee/episodes/5a781ce0-f80e-4a08-a13c-ca2ffb3d0c7a/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee&awEpisodeId=5a781ce0-f80e-4a08-a13c-ca2ffb3d0c7a",
        "durationSec": 4125,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      },
      {
        "recordId": "bibleproject:podcast:beginning",
        "startSec": 680,
        "endSec": 800,
        "why": "This clip shows how the allusion works beyond the first line. The hosts read John through “Genesis 1,” with light entering darkness, and then through “God coming to dwell with his people in the tabernacle.” That gives you the two major lenses for John 1: creation and divine presence.",
        "episodeTitle": "In the Beginning – John 1",
        "sourceId": "bibleproject",
        "source": "BibleProject",
        "audioUrl": "https://afp-597195-injected.calisto.simplecastaudio.com/695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee/episodes/8f0c5975-65cf-4a02-baf0-786ba6649656/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee&awEpisodeId=8f0c5975-65cf-4a02-baf0-786ba6649656",
        "durationSec": 3671,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      },
      {
        "recordId": "spoken-gospel:podcast:3c0fc244-3dc3-11f1-ab33-5f07c6c92de3",
        "startSec": 2860,
        "endSec": 3210,
        "why": "Now listen for John’s whole-Gospel structure. The speakers trace seven days through John 1–2, ending in a wedding, and explain that the seven signs point toward an eighth: “Jesus’ resurrection. New creation.” They also connect the eighth day with leaving old creation behind and beginning new creation.",
        "episodeTitle": "Gospel of John Overview: A Unique Eyewitness",
        "sourceId": "spoken-gospel",
        "source": "Spoken Gospel",
        "audioUrl": "https://traffic.megaphone.fm/SPG5222140559.mp3",
        "durationSec": 3787,
        "adInsertionDrift": true
      },
      {
        "recordId": "ask-nt-wright:podcast:e1d1cb1c-1ba2-11f0-9e6a-730b0b3fac80",
        "startSec": 580,
        "endSec": 760,
        "why": "This brings the Genesis pattern to John 20. Wright highlights John’s repeated phrase “the first day of the week” and calls it “the beginning of God’s new creation,” then links Jesus breathing on the disciples with God breathing life into Adam in Genesis 2. New creation therefore includes a Spirit-given vocation for the church.",
        "episodeTitle": "BONUS Subscriber only Easter Show: What does Easter mean for the mission of the Church today? Tom Wright and Mike Bird",
        "sourceId": "ask-nt-wright",
        "source": "Ask NT Wright Anything",
        "audioUrl": "https://traffic.megaphone.fm/NSR4249819305.mp3?updated=1749648274",
        "durationSec": 1578,
        "adInsertionDrift": true
      },
      {
        "recordId": "bibleproject:podcast:heaven-earth-part-3",
        "startSec": 1030,
        "endSec": 1210,
        "why": "End by widening the lens from John’s symbols to their destination. The hosts describe “the new Eden, the new creation, where heaven and earth overlap fully again because of Jesus,” and show how garden, city, temple, river, and tree-of-life imagery converge in the final renewal.",
        "episodeTitle": "Jesus, The Ultimate Heaven & Earth Meeting Place",
        "sourceId": "bibleproject",
        "source": "BibleProject",
        "audioUrl": "https://afp-597195-injected.calisto.simplecastaudio.com/695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee/episodes/9327a394-42a0-4eaf-a203-09e63e82aacd/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee&awEpisodeId=9327a394-42a0-4eaf-a203-09e63e82aacd",
        "durationSec": 2514,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      }
    ],
    "closing": "Taken together, these clips suggest that John’s Genesis allusions are not decorative references. They frame Jesus as the agent and embodiment of creation, present his resurrection as the beginning of the eighth-day world, and invite you to read the Gospel as new creation already breaking into the old.",
    "totalSeconds": 970
  },
